# Context

## Why This Way
The runtime sits in @oal/runner, not @oal/gateway: it owns the
trial database, the wall clock, and the batch plan, which the
gateway must never see. The gateway keeps only the two handles
(ScenarioBackend, GatewayState) landed in 5c0ff5d.

## Gotchas
- packReference filters by role AND pointer; the same path can
  carry two references (text copy vs parsed schema).
- The wire-trust check on backendApiVersion needs a widened
  local: the declared type pins the literal 1, so a direct
  comparison is flagged dead by lint.
- VirtualClock.now() returns an RFC 3339 string, not a number;
  CommittedSemanticEvent.logicalTime is already formatted.

